  "question": {
    "choices": [
      "A. Both groups yielded more than 200 grams of tomatoes, but Group A produced significantly more than Group B.",
      "B. The yield of tomatoes was lower in Group A compared to Group B, contradicting the hypothesis.",
      "C. Group A with organic fertilizer yielded around 400 grams, while Group B yielded nearly 600 grams.",
      "D. The plants in Group A produced more tomatoes than those in Group B, supporting the hypothesis that organic fertilizer is more effective."
    ],
    "correct_answer": [
      "D"
    ],
    "explanation": "Choice D is the best answer because it accurately reflects the data shown in the graph, indicating that the yield of tomatoes from the group using organic fertilizer (Group A) was higher than that from the group using synthetic fertilizer (Group B). Specifically, Group A yielded around 700 grams while Group B yielded around 400 grams. This supports the hypothesis that organic fertilizer is more effective in increasing yield compared to synthetic fertilizer. \n\nChoice A is misleading because, while it correctly states that both groups exceeded 200 grams, it does not explicitly mention the significant difference in yield that favors Group A. \n\nChoice B contradicts the data, as it incorrectly claims that Group A yielded less than Group B, which is not supported by the graph. \n\nChoice C incorrectly states the yield figures for Group A, claiming it yielded around 400 grams instead of the actual 700 grams, which undermines the validity of the claim.",
    "paragraph": "<p>In an effort to understand the impact of different types of fertilizers on crop yield, a team of agronomists conducted an experiment comparing organic and synthetic fertilizers. The researchers planted two groups of tomato plants, with one group receiving organic fertilizer while the other group received synthetic fertilizer. After a growing period of eight weeks, the researchers measured the weight of the harvested tomatoes. The hypothesis posited by the researchers was that organic fertilizer would lead to a higher yield compared to synthetic fertilizer.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"image\">\n<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"568.280625pt\" height=\"425.046668pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 568.280625 425.046668\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\">\n <metadata>\n  <rdf:RDF xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:cc=\"http://creativecommons.org/ns#\" xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\">\n   <cc:Work>\n    <dc:type rdf:resource=\"http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/StillImage\"/>\n    <dc:date>2026-02-22T09:45:59.545443</dc:date>\n    <dc:format>image/svg+xml</dc:format>\n    <dc:creator>\n     <cc:Agent>\n      <dc:title>Matplotlib v3.10.8, https://matplotlib.org/</dc:title>\n     </cc:Agent>\n    </dc:creator>\n   </cc:Work>\n  </rdf:RDF>\n </metadata>\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 425.046668 \nL 568.280625 425.046668 \nL 568.280625 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: #ffffff\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 50.980625 372.883035 \nL 561.080625 372.883035 \nL 561.080625 23.077969 \nL 50.980625 23.077969 \nz\n\" style=\"fill: #ffffff\"/>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 74.166989 372.883035 \nL 169.640251 372.883035 \nL 169.640251 23.077969 \nL 74.166989 23.077969 \nz\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p6e4d50f486)\" style=\"f